# Module F Demo Checklist

## Functional deliverables
- [x] Access-history dashboard with institution, document, timestamp, purpose, action, consent status
- [x] Search and filter audit records by institution, document, purpose, or consent status
- [x] Consent expiry status and notification summary in the app
- [x] Expired audit record anonymization workflow for retention governance
- [x] Demo seeding of sample audit + consent data for a test patient
- [x] API routes registered in the backend startup

## Backend validation
- [ ] Start backend with `uvicorn main:app --reload`
- [ ] Verify `/api/audit/` returns seeded records
- [ ] Verify `/api/audit/consent-status` returns active/expiring/expired counts
- [ ] Run cleanup endpoint `/api/audit/expired/anonymize`

## Frontend validation
- [ ] Start frontend with `npm run dev`
- [ ] Sign in as a patient
- [ ] Open `/audit` and confirm records render
- [ ] Try search/filter controls and retention cleanup button

## Deployment notes
- [ ] Ensure `DATABASE_URL` is set in backend `.env`
- [ ] Ensure Tesseract is installed for scanned document OCR if needed
- [ ] Use a production-safe DB and secure CORS config before release

## Demo narrative
1. Patient reviews access history and sees institution-level access entries.
2. Consent summary highlights any soon-to-expire or expired consent records.
3. Retention cleanup anonymizes stale expired records according to policy.
4. Platform demonstrates transparency, lifecycle governance, and privacy accountability.
